# Logistic Regression Project

##  Overview
This project was developed as part of my academic coursework, where I implemented a complete machine learning pipeline using Logistic Regression.  
The goal of this project was to understand how different steps like data preprocessing, visualization, feature selection, and model evaluation work together to build a reliable classification model.

---

##  Dataset
The dataset used in this project is sourced from Kaggle.



This dataset contains multiple features that are used to predict the target variable.

---

##  Steps Performed

- Data Loading  
- Basic Data Understanding (head, info, describe)  
- Data Cleaning (handling missing values)  
- Encoding (Label Encoding / One-Hot Encoding)  
- Data Visualization (countplot, heatmap, etc.)  
- Feature Selection  
- Train-Test Split  
- Feature Scaling (StandardScaler)  
- Model Training using Logistic Regression  
- Prediction on test data  
- Model Evaluation (Accuracy, Confusion Matrix, Classification Report)  
- Comparison of Actual vs Predicted values  

---

##  Results

-  Accuracy: **82%**  
- The model performs well on unseen data and gives reliable predictions.

